"with this structure directly. Instead, clk operations flow through the "
"framework and the framework manipulates this structure to keep track of "
"parent/child relationships, rate, enable state, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk.rst:48
msgid ""
"The members above make up the core of the clk tree topology.  The clk api "
"itself defines several driver-facing functions which operate on struct clk.  "
"That api is documented in include/linux/clk.h."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk.rst:52
msgid ""
"Platforms and devices utilizing the common struct clk_core use the struct "
"clk_ops pointer in struct clk_core to perform the hardware-specific parts of "
"the operations defined in clk-provider.h, and can set one or more framework-"
"level flags documented below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:121
msgid ""
"Callback operations for hardware clocks; these are to be provided by the "
"clock implementation, and will be called by drivers through the clk_* api."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:125
msgid "``prepare``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:126
msgid ""
"Prepare the clock for enabling. This must not return until the clock is "
"fully prepared, and it's safe to call clk_enable. This callback is intended "
"to allow clock implementations to do any initialisation that may sleep. "
"Called with prepare_lock held."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:131
msgid "``unprepare``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:132
msgid ""
"Release the clock from its prepared state. This will typically undo any work "
"done in the **prepare** callback. Called with prepare_lock held."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:135
msgid "``is_prepared``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:136
msgid ""
"Queries the hardware to determine if the clock is prepared. This function is "
"allowed to sleep. Optional, if this op is not set then the prepare count "
"will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:139
msgid "``unprepare_unused``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:140
msgid ""
"Unprepare the clock atomically.  Only called from clk_disable_unused for "
"prepare clocks with special needs. Called with prepare mutex held. This "
"function may sleep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:143
msgid "``enable``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:144
msgid ""
"Enable the clock atomically. This must not return until the clock is "
"generating a valid clock signal, usable by consumer devices. Called with "
"enable_lock held. This function must not sleep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:148
msgid "``disable``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:149
msgid ""
"Disable the clock atomically. Called with enable_lock held. This function "
"must not sleep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:151
msgid "``is_enabled``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:152
msgid ""
"Queries the hardware to determine if the clock is enabled. This function "
"must not sleep. Optional, if this op is not set then the enable count will "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:155
msgid "``disable_unused``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:156
msgid ""
"Disable the clock atomically.  Only called from clk_disable_unused for gate "
"clocks with special needs. Called with enable_lock held.  This function must "
"not sleep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:160
msgid "``save_context``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:161
msgid "Save the context of the clock in prepration for poweroff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:162
msgid "``restore_context``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:163
msgid "Restore the context of the clock after a restoration of power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:165
msgid "``recalc_rate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:166
msgid ""
"Recalculate the rate of this clock, by querying hardware. The parent rate is "
"an input parameter.  It is up to the caller to ensure that the prepare_mutex "
"is held across this call. If the driver cannot figure out a rate for this "
"clock, it must return 0. Returns the calculated rate. Optional, but "
"recommended - if this op is not set then clock rate will be initialized to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:172
msgid "``determine_rate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:173
msgid ""
"Given a target rate as input, returns the closest rate actually supported by "
"the clock, and optionally the parent clock that should be used to provide "
"the clock rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:176
msgid "``set_parent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:177
msgid ""
"Change the input source of this clock; for clocks with multiple possible "
"parents specify a new parent by passing in the index as a u8 corresponding "
"to the parent in either the .parent_names or .parents arrays.  This function "
"in affect translates an array index into the value programmed into the "
"hardware. Returns 0 on success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:183
msgid "``get_parent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:184
msgid ""
"Queries the hardware to determine the parent of a clock.  The return value "
"is a u8 which specifies the index corresponding to the parent clock.  This "
"index can be applied to either the .parent_names or .parents arrays.  In "
"short, this function translates the parent value read from hardware into an "
"array index.  Currently only called when the clock is initialized by "
"__clk_init.  This callback is mandatory for clocks with multiple parents.  "
"It is optional (and unnecessary) for clocks with 0 or 1 parents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:193
msgid "``set_rate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:194
msgid ""
"Change the rate of this clock. The requested rate is specified by the second "
"argument, which should typically be the return of .determine_rate call.  The "
"third argument gives the parent rate which is likely helpful for most ."
"set_rate implementation. Returns 0 on success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:199
msgid "``set_rate_and_parent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:200
msgid ""
"Change the rate and the parent of this clock. The requested rate is "
"specified by the second argument, which should typically be the return of "
"clk_round_rate() call.  The third argument gives the parent rate which is "
"likely helpful for most .set_rate_and_parent implementation. The fourth "
"argument gives the parent index. This callback is optional (and unnecessary) "
"for clocks with 0 or 1 parents as well as for clocks that can tolerate "
"switching the rate and the parent separately via calls to .set_parent and ."
"set_rate. Returns 0 on success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:210
msgid "``set_spread_spectrum``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:211
msgid ""
"Optional callback used to configure the spread spectrum modulation "
"frequency, percentage, and method to reduce EMI by spreading the clock "
"frequency over a wider range. Returns 0 on success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:216
msgid "``recalc_accuracy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:217
msgid ""
"Recalculate the accuracy of this clock. The clock accuracy is expressed in "
"ppb (parts per billion). The parent accuracy is an input parameter. Returns "
"the calculated accuracy.  Optional - if this op is not set then clock "
"accuracy will be initialized to parent accuracy or 0 (perfect clock) if "
"clock has no parent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:223
msgid "``get_phase``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:224
msgid ""
"Queries the hardware to get the current phase of a clock. Returned values "
"are 0-359 degrees on success, negative error codes on failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:227
msgid "``set_phase``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:228
msgid ""
"Shift the phase this clock signal in degrees specified by the second "
"argument. Valid values for degrees are 0-359. Return 0 on success, otherwise "
"-EERROR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:231
msgid "``get_duty_cycle``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:232
msgid ""
"Queries the hardware to get the current duty cycle ratio of a clock. "
"Returned values denominator cannot be 0 and must be superior or equal to the "
"numerator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:235
msgid "``set_duty_cycle``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:236
msgid ""
"Apply the duty cycle ratio to this clock signal specified by the numerator "
"(2nd argurment) and denominator (3rd  argument). Argument must be a valid "
"ratio (denominator > 0 and >= numerator) Return 0 on success, otherwise -"
"EERROR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:240
msgid "``init``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:241
msgid ""
"Perform platform-specific initialization magic. This is not used by any of "
"the basic clock types. This callback exist for HW which needs to perform "
"some initialisation magic for CCF to get an accurate view of the clock. It "
"may also be used dynamic resource allocation is required. It shall not used "
"to deal with clock parameters, such as rate or parents. Returns 0 on "
"success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:249
msgid "``terminate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:250
msgid "Free any resource allocated by init."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:251
msgid "``debug_init``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:252
msgid ""
"Set up type-specific debugfs entries for this clock.  This is called once, "
"after the debugfs directory entry for this clock has been created.  The "
"dentry pointer representing that directory is provided as an argument.  "
"Called with prepare_lock held.  Returns 0 on success, -EERROR otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:256
msgid ""
"The clk_enable/clk_disable and clk_prepare/clk_unprepare pairs allow "
"implementations to split any work between atomic (enable) and sleepable "
"(prepare) contexts.  If enabling a clock requires code that might sleep, "
"this must be done in clk_prepare.  Clock enable code that will never be "
"called in a sleepable context may be implemented in clk_enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:57: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:262
msgid ""
"Typically, drivers will call clk_prepare when a clock may be needed later "
"(eg. when a device is opened), and clk_enable when the clock is actually "
"required (eg. from an interrupt). Note that clk_prepare MUST have been "
"called before clk_enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk.rst:61
msgid "Core flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:63: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:14
msgid ""
"Flags used across common struct clk. These flags should only affect the top-"
"level framework. Custom flags for dealing with hardware specifics belong in "
"struct clk_foo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:63: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:18
msgid "CLK_SET_RATE_GATE - must be gated across rate change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:63: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:19
msgid "CLK_SET_PARENT_GATE - must be gated across re-parent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/clk:63: ../include/linux/clk-provider.h:20
msgid "CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT - propagate rate change up one level"
